course: dictionary
lesson: 13290
title: Words for old machines
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gramophone is an old machine that plays music from records. A record is a flat disc with grooves cut into it, and the machine turns it round to make the sound. «Grandma wound up the gramophone, and the music began.» The clue is wound up: the machine had to be turned by hand before it could play.
explain: Look at the big horn on the gramophone. «The horn made the music loud enough for the whole room to hear.» The words around gramophone tell you the horn is for making sound louder, so you can picture the machine even if you have never seen one.
explain: Try the swap check. «The family gathered round the gramophone.» Put in «the old music machine» instead, and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A gramophone is an old machine for playing music from records.
fact: A record is a flat disc with grooves that carry the sound.
fact: Gramophones came before radio, cassettes, CDs and streaming.
fact: Emile Berliner invented the gramophone with flat discs, and Thomas Edison invented the phonograph.
fact: «Wind up the gramophone» means turn the handle so the machine has the power to play.
exercise: «Grandma wound up the gramophone.» What is a gramophone? | *An old machine for playing music from records | A plant with big, wide leaves | A phone for calling family | A tool for baking bread
exercise: The gramophone has a big horn. What was the horn for? | *To make the music louder | To take the sound out of the room | To hold the records | To keep the machine cool
exercise: Which of these came after the gramophone in the story of music? | Candles | Horse and cart | *Radio | Handwritten letters
test: «The family gathered round the gramophone to hear a song.» What does gramophone mean? | A wooden chair | *An old machine for playing records | A type of cooking pot | A bicycle with a bell
test: Who invented the gramophone with flat discs? | Leo | Grandma | Thomas Edison | *Emile Berliner
exam: Jayden meets the word gramophone in a new book. What should he do first? | Look only at the first letter | *Read the words around it for clues | Guess a random word | Skip it and forget the whole sentence
